1832
01:26:16,000 --> 01:26:20,000
See to it they get the necessary hereditary genes they need.

1833
01:26:20,000 --> 01:26:23,000
Do you suppose we could repair the machine, perfect it?

1834
01:26:24,000 --> 01:26:26,000
So that a man could travel through and return?

1835
01:26:26,000 --> 01:26:28,000
I won't have a boyfriend!

1836
01:26:28,000 --> 01:26:32,000
Others like her will come. There may be millions of them.

1837
01:26:32,000 --> 01:26:34,000
Boy!

1838
01:26:34,000 --> 01:26:36,000
We've got to do something clear after all we are human beings.

1839
01:26:36,000 --> 01:26:38,000
You're right, Buzz.

1840
01:26:38,000 --> 01:26:40,000
So you do it.

1841
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:42,000
But there's another way.

1842
01:26:42,000 --> 01:26:44,000
Ham?

1843
01:26:44,000 --> 01:26:46,000
The future is what we make it.

1844
01:26:46,000 --> 01:26:48,000
Wait a minute, I'm full of crap.

1845
01:26:48,000 --> 01:26:50,000
Whether there will be creatures like her.

1846
01:26:50,000 --> 01:26:52,000
I like milk!

1847
01:26:53,000 --> 01:26:54,000
Especially you, Bob.

1848
01:26:54,000 --> 01:26:57,000
All of us.

1849
01:26:57,000 --> 01:26:59,000
On mankind.

1850
01:26:59,000 --> 01:27:01,000
On what we do.

1851
01:27:01,000 --> 01:27:08,000
Remember, moisturize and use a sunscreen!

1852
01:27:08,000 --> 01:27:11,000
And don't bob for french fries.

1853
01:27:11,000 --> 01:27:14,000
Marry only UL approved attractive people!

1854
01:27:14,000 --> 01:27:19,000
Good night!

1855
01:27:19,000 --> 01:27:20,000
Good night!

1856
01:27:20,000 --> 01:27:34,000
Jeez, what's the big deal, Mike?

1857
01:27:34,000 --> 01:27:37,000
It's nothing. I just want to know how many times you took Ginger out.

1858
01:27:37,000 --> 01:27:42,000
Well, I didn't exactly take her out, if you know what I mean, my friend.

1859
01:27:42,000 --> 01:27:46,000
You didn't exactly take her out, you mean you.

1860
01:27:47,000 --> 01:27:49,000
I'm a Dutch treat, my friend.

1861
01:27:49,000 --> 01:27:53,000
So you fancy yourself as something of a ladies man, then?

1862
01:27:53,000 --> 01:27:58,000
Oh, I think the ladies themselves fancy me as something of a ladies man, my friend.

1863
01:27:58,000 --> 01:28:02,000
So what if I set you up on a blind date with a real hot tomato?

1864
01:28:02,000 --> 01:28:06,000
Well, I think I could handle it, my friend, my friend.

1865
01:28:06,000 --> 01:28:09,000
Alrighty, then you think you could be ready in...

1866
01:28:09,000 --> 01:28:15,000
Ready, willing and able, Mike.

1867
01:28:16,000 --> 01:28:18,000
Just dial her up here and...

1868
01:28:18,000 --> 01:28:21,000
Wow, he's going to bring you honey from across time!

1869
01:28:21,000 --> 01:28:23,000
Maybe Theo Patcher or Mary Todd Lincoln!

1870
01:28:23,000 --> 01:28:26,000
Or all of the gold diggers of 1933, maybe!

1871
01:28:26,000 --> 01:28:28,000
Bring 'em all on, my friend!

1872
01:28:28,000 --> 01:28:30,000
And we're all set!

1873
01:28:30,000 --> 01:28:33,000
Whoa! Get away from me! Get away from me!

1874
01:28:33,000 --> 01:28:40,000
Oh, Mike, that is rich! I guess I needed a little lesson.

1875
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:42,000
Oh, that's great.

1876
01:28:42,000 --> 01:28:44,000
So, where to, sweetie?

1877
01:28:45,000 --> 01:28:48,000
Perkins it is, then! Bread, bowl, salads for two!

1878
01:28:48,000 --> 01:28:53,000
Alright, have fun! And hey, don't let her rip your face off!

1879
01:28:53,000 --> 01:28:55,000
I won't! Mike, the peepers won't!

1880
01:28:55,000 --> 01:28:57,000
Ah, that was a good one.

1881
01:28:57,000 --> 01:29:00,000
Please, we are not peepers, we're observers.

1882
01:29:00,000 --> 01:29:02,000
There is a victor!

1883
01:29:02,000 --> 01:29:03,000
Excellent! Give her the sword!

1884
01:29:03,000 --> 01:29:06,000
Now, you must vanquish your opponent.

1885
01:29:06,000 --> 01:29:08,000
Vanquish, shway?

1886
01:29:08,000 --> 01:29:09,000
You have earned his death.

1887
01:29:09,000 --> 01:29:12,000
Well, I'd really just rather have an all-sport.

1888
01:29:13,000 --> 01:29:16,000
By our law that you terminate the hairy one. Use the sword!

1889
01:29:16,000 --> 01:29:18,000
Well, okay.

1890
01:29:18,000 --> 01:29:29,000
No. I won't.

1891
01:29:29,000 --> 01:29:32,000
It is required by your laws, not ours.

1892
01:29:32,000 --> 01:29:34,000
We are human.

1893
01:29:34,000 --> 01:29:38,000
We may not have evolved to your level of intelligence yet.

1894
01:29:38,000 --> 01:29:42,000
And yes, we often stumble in our quest to do right.

1895
01:29:42,000 --> 01:29:44,000
But at least we strive for compassion.

1896
01:29:44,000 --> 01:29:46,000
For kindness.

1897
01:29:46,000 --> 01:29:49,000
And yes, for love.

1898
01:29:49,000 --> 01:29:52,000
There, I've said it and I wouldn't take it back.

1899
01:29:52,000 --> 01:29:58,000
Being human isn't about killing in cold blood those who are helpless.

1900
01:29:58,000 --> 01:30:01,000
Though I have in fact done that, I probably shouldn't have.

1901
01:30:01,000 --> 01:30:05,000
Being human is about watching the sun rise and set.

1902
01:30:05,000 --> 01:30:11,000
About the quality of mercy and yes, again, about love.

1903
01:30:13,000 --> 01:30:19,000
Being human isn't about eating lots of pills and carrying your brain around in a salad bowl.

1904
01:30:19,000 --> 01:30:24,000
Being human is about the feeling one gets when you see what you do.

1905
01:30:24,000 --> 01:30:27,000
You forgot I'm not human!

1906
01:30:27,000 --> 01:30:31,000
Oh, that tears it, Megillah. You are so dead, I can't believe it!

1907
01:30:31,000 --> 01:30:35,000
It may be time to end this, Observers.

1908
01:30:35,000 --> 01:30:37,000
Shall I schedule the dissections?

1909
01:30:37,000 --> 01:30:39,000
Excellent idea, Observers.

1910
01:30:40,000 --> 01:30:42,000
Thank you, Observer. And you too, Observer.

1911
01:30:42,000 --> 01:30:44,000
Tune in next week.

1912
01:30:44,000 --> 01:30:46,000
Observe your local listings.

1913
01:30:46,000 --> 01:30:49,000
I'll skewer you, you big sticky cheater!

